# ⛔ NARROW RULES, EACH ON ONE DIRECTORY ONLY: THE NARROWNESS IS THE POINT.
# ⚠️ RECALL OF 2026-10-09 -- audit of 2026-09-30, AUD-1123, AUD-1126.
# ⚠️ RECALL OF 2026-10-14 -- audit of 2026-09-30, AUD-732: these comments are in English, as are
# those of every other configuration file of the repository; the rules are unchanged.
#
# The frozen bytes of the durable record (`crates/kernel/tests/frozen/*.cbor`) are the only
# artefact of the project that is never regenerated: if they change it is not an update, it is a
# change of format. A `text=auto` that treated them as text could rewrite a `0d 0a` into `0a`
# between the working tree and the index, and the file would come back DIFFERENT from the one
# that was measured -- with the oracle red and nobody to blame.
#
# ⚠️ RECALL OF 2026-09-01: this line said "NONE OF THE **THREE** FILES" and the files were four;
# the fifth arrived with task 6 of milestone 6. ⛔ The numeral is REMOVED and not realigned --
# gotcha #31, and the remedy is a subtraction: how many there are is what
# `ls crates/kernel/tests/frozen/*.cbor` says, which does not rot.
# ⚠️ TODAY NONE OF THE FROZEN FILES CONTAINS A `0a` OR A `0d`, and they contain `00` besides, which
# is enough for git to recognise them as binary by itself. ⛔ BUT THAT IS AN ACCIDENT OF THE
# CONTENT AND NOT A GUARANTEE: a frozen record of tomorrow can carry those bytes, and then the
# protection would be needed and would not be there. Declared now, while it costs one line.
#
# ⛔ AND NO `* text=auto`, EVER, in this file. The line endings of this repository are MIXED PER
# FILE -- there is no convention to follow, there is a file not to change -- and a global rule
# would normalise sources nobody touched, declaring hundreds of lines changed in `git diff`. It
# has already happened twice, with a script; from a `.gitattributes` it would be worse, because
# nobody rereads it.
crates/kernel/tests/frozen/*.cbor binary

# ⛔ THE FIXTURES OF THE `ipc` WIRE -- THE SECOND RULE, AND THE NARROWNESS STILL HOLDS.
#
# `gui/schema/fixtures/` was born with task 3 of sub-project 2. The `.json` files carry the
# EXPECTED VALUE of every variant, and `the_committed_fixtures_match_the_schema` compares them
# BYTE FOR BYTE with what `variant_json` produces, which always ends in a single `\n`. With
# `core.autocrlf=true` -- a setting of the MACHINE and not of the repository, and its value on the
# machine being worked on is what `git config --show-origin --get core.autocrlf` says -- a fresh
# checkout would rewrite them in CRLF, and the check would go red on ALL of them: green where they
# were written, red on every clone.
# ⚠️ RECALL OF 2026-10-09 -- audit of 2026-09-30, AUD-1125.
# ✅ MEASURED ON 2026-09-17 and not deduced: `git checkout-index -a --prefix=<dir>/` gives **14**
# CRs in the `.json` files against **0** in the working tree. The map held by itself, because
# `str::lines()` strips the `\r`; the `.json` files do not, because the comparison is on bytes.
#
# ⚠️ AND THE `.bin` FILES ARE THE SAME STORY AS THE `.cbor` ABOVE: today git recognises them as
# binary by itself -- `i/-text` in `git ls-files --eol 'gui/schema/fixtures/*.bin'` --, and a `00`
# is enough for it, as a `0d` that does not precede a `0a` would be. The byte the protection saves
# is the `0a`: a read as text would rewrite it into `0d 0a` at checkout with `core.autocrlf=true`,
# and some `.bin` files already carry it -- which ones is what `wc -l gui/schema/fixtures/*.bin`
# says, as it counts the `0a`. The protection would really be needed the day git stopped
# recognising them by itself, and that is an accident of the content, as it is up there.
# ⚠️ RECALL OF 2026-10-09 -- audit of 2026-09-30, AUD-1127.
#
# ⛔ AND A `* text=auto` STAYS FORBIDDEN: these three lines name ONE directory, which is the point.
gui/schema/fixtures/*.bin  binary
gui/schema/fixtures/*.json text eol=lf
gui/schema/fixtures/*.map  text eol=lf
